tags: celaut-instances

A kind of network: the instances of celaut services that declare the same network. The
service author selects the keys of the value, to name the domain.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key, separated by a newline, with no repeated
key. The node does not read the keys. Example: app=chat-room and room=main.

Two instances are in the same network only if their networks have equal domains (the
formal and the value, after the settings of the network). The node finds the members
in its own instances and in the instances of the peers that it knows. A member gives
the ports of its API whose layers match Service.Network.protocol_stack. The node is
bound.

=== formal
class=domain
members=the instances, of this node and of the peers that it knows, whose service declares a network with an equal domain after its settings; on the ports of their API whose layers match the protocol stack of the network
name=celaut-instances
value=key=value lines sorted by key, with no repeated key; the node compares the bytes and does not read the keys
